package cli

import (
	"fmt"
)

const nativeS6ProfessionalFormat = "\nUse Claude Code native worktree isolation from Main HEAD %s. Normal delivery: save the following professional JSON files relative to your actual worktree; do not write these drafts into Main. Plan before implementation; save does not activate anything. Implement, self-test, commit only actual TASK products and save Result. Keep these private professional files out of Git; do not force-add them. Return this exact brief reference %s and the absolute path to your Result.\n\nPlan: %s\n```json\n{\"objective\":null,\"planned_paths\":[],\"assertion_checks\":[{\"assertion\":null,\"oracle\":null,\"done_when_indexes\":[]}],\"risks_blockers\":[]}\n```\nPlan fields are objective, planned_paths, assertion_checks and risks_blockers only. Plan.risks_blockers is an array of strings. Registered dependencies are system facts, not a private Plan question. Each assertion has assertion, oracle and done_when_indexes (zero-based indices into Done when). Cover each required condition.\n\nResult: %s\n```json\n{\"summary\":null,\"assertion_evidence\":[{\"plan_assertion_index\":0,\"evidence_refs\":[]}],\"risks_blockers\":[],\"scope_deviations\":[],\"closing_assessment\":{\"disposition\":null,\"conditions\":[{\"done_when_index\":0,\"judgment\":null,\"rationale\":null}]}}\n```\nResult fields are summary, assertion_evidence, risks_blockers, scope_deviations and closing_assessment only. Result has no dependencies field. Use exactly the shown field names; no extra nested fields. Each assertion_evidence item names its zero-based plan_assertion_index in your actual Plan and supplies evidence_refs describing your actual observation or available source. Commands, output and professional descriptions are acceptable; cite a real file when useful, without creating one just for reception. Record what you actually ran and observed in summary or closing rationale. Reception does not prove execution; Main performs its own integration checks. Result.risks_blockers and Result.scope_deviations are arrays of strings. Report real risks, blockers, assumptions, limitations and scope deviations honestly; retain your original wording for Main to consider against the TASK and actual changes. Nonempty lists alone do not determine completion or approval. Express truly unfinished or blocked work in your existing closing disposition and conditions. Replace nulls with your own professional answers; do not copy placeholder values. closing_assessment has disposition (complete/incomplete/blocked) and conditions; each condition has done_when_index, judgment (satisfied/incomplete/blocked) and rationale. The receiver derives its plan_assertion_indexes from your Plan's done_when_indexes; you do not copy that mapping. Existing full assertion/oracle evidence rows and explicit plan_assertion_indexes remain valid when they exactly satisfy the original Plan; explicit values are never corrected automatically. Do not mix plan_assertion_index with assertion/oracle in one row. Cover each Plan assertion exactly once and each Done when condition exactly once. Include real self-check commands/results in summary. For real blockers, use the separate blocked handoff below instead of fabricating completed checks or evidence.\n"

// The same minimal handoff is shown before work and in missing-artifact feedback.
// It is professional blocker information, never a completion report.
func nativeS6BlockerInstructions(result string) string {
	return fmt.Sprintf("\nBlocked handoff, before or after forming a Plan: save a Result at %s with this minimum shape:\n```json\n{\"summary\":null,\"risks_blockers\":[null],\"closing_assessment\":{\"disposition\":\"blocked\"}}\n```\nReplace summary with actual progress and unfinished work, and risks_blockers with nonempty strings naming the real blockers. If no Plan can be formed, no Plan or assertion evidence is required for this handoff. If a Plan or real evidence already exists, preserve it; save the minimum Result shown here without assertion_evidence, scope_deviations or conditions; keep existing evidence files and describe their location in summary. Return the original exact brief and the absolute Result path, and state the actual blocker in your native return. Main owns recovery of the original responsibility. This minimal shape creates no acceptance or completion receipt, integration or stage completion. An existing full Result (including a blocked one) keeps its original Plan, evidence and condition validation and may be received as unfinished work; it cannot satisfy completion or integration while blocked.\n", result)
}

// Append current guidance without changing any exact-byte historical format.
const nativeS6CurrentAuthoringGuidance = "\nPlan.planned_paths is this Assignment's write set: actual product or test paths you intend to change, within its registered effective write scope. Exclude read-only inputs and private Plan/Result files. Commit actual TASK product changes; an empty commit supplies no changed product or implementation evidence and cannot replace unfinished work. Saving private Plan/Result files alone does not prove reception or integration; return the exact original references for SubagentStop, and follow the original reception diagnostics. Saving a private Plan/Result or returning its path does not establish reception. Only the original consumer receipt confirms acceptance; Main can query loop-harness s6 status --root <Main-root> for unreceived results and reception advice. Preserve the same Worker and artifacts if reception is pending.\n"
